{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", collected by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"]},{"text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6576_6E74"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the set for its users:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and calls LinkerSets’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that imports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “no macro named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API (","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvents.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set is read in one place.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}]},{"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}]},{"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type, is refused with a message, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"reference"},{"text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}]},{"text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Routes"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", read as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<Route>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Migrations","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)"},{"type":"text","text":", read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>"},{"type":"text","text":", sorted by a version the migration declares."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency registrations"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Finding records"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}]},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"title":"LinkerSetKind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Performance"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","role":"symbol","title":"LinkerSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","role":"article","title":"What the macros refuse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}]}}}